 "intro_html": "Nagoya’s favourite rice ball: a <b>whole shrimp tempura</b>, dipped in mentsuyu so the crisp, thick batter soaks up the sauce, hidden inside a small salted rice triangle with its <b>red tail sticking out of the top</b>. A strip of nori crosses over the front like the collar of a kimono. They’re small — two or three bites each — so you eat them by the handful. This is Just One Cookbook’s recipe; for the rice and shaping basics see <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a>.",
