 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cook the rice in the water — rice cooker or pot (see <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a>). <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1.5\" data-s=\"0\">1½ cups</span> of uncooked rice makes about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"660\" data-s=\"0\">660 g</span> of cooked rice: 12 tenmusu.</li><li>While it cooks, make the tempura (steps 2–7).</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cook the rice",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/tenmusu/1.webp?v=f9a75efc38",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": "Rice",
   "part_id": "part-rice",
   "time": "~45 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~45 min</span>",
   "title": "Cook the rice",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1.5\">1½ cups</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"300\" data-alt=\"1\">300 g</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Japanese short-grain white rice"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1.6667\">1⅔ cups</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"400\" data-alt=\"1\">400 ml</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Water (for the rice)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Peel off the shells — easiest starting from the third segment — but <b>leave the tail on</b> (see notes).</li><li>Run a skewer under the dark vein along the back and lift it out.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Peel and devein the shrimp",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Peel the shell off, starting at the third segment — leave the tail on.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/2-how1.webp?v=6d0566e0d0"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Lift the vein out with a skewer.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/2-how2.webp?v=368f9dd3cc"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/2.webp?v=9ba19991a0",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Shrimp tempura",
   "part_id": "part-shrimp-tempura",
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Peel and devein the shrimp",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"12\" data-n=\"2\">12</span>",
     "name_html": "Medium shrimp, shell on"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Shrimp in a bowl with the starch and a little water; rub them with your hands — a common Japanese trick that makes them plumper.</li><li>Pour off the grey water, rinse a couple of times under cold running water, drain and pat <b>dry</b> with paper towels.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rub with starch, rinse, dry",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rub the shrimp with the starch and a little water, then rinse.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/3-how1.webp?v=03b2178593"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Pat them very dry.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/3-how2.webp?v=8464759494"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/3.webp?v=35547dff00",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": "Shrimp tempura",
   "part_id": "part-shrimp-tempura",
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Rub with starch, rinse, dry",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Potato starch or cornstarch (to clean the shrimp)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Heat the oil to <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"170\" data-b=\"180\" data-s=\"0\">170–180 °C</span></b> in a small, deep pot — small enough that <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 cups</span> are deep enough to fry in.</p>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Heat the oil",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/tenmusu/4.webp?v=e42004207b",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": "Shrimp tempura",
   "part_id": "part-shrimp-tempura",
   "time": "~8 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~8 min</span>",
   "title": "Heat the oil",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"2\">2 cups</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"480\" data-alt=\"1\">480 ml</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Neutral oil (for deep-frying)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Sift the cake flour and starch through a fine-mesh strainer into a bowl — it makes the batter lighter and crisper.</li><li>Add:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>ice water <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.3333\">⅓ cup</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"80\" data-alt=\"1\">80 ml</span>)</span></span></li><li>rice vinegar (unseasoned) <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ tbsp</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Mix only briefly: lumps are fine. It should be <b>thick, like fritter batter</b> — thick batter soaks up more sauce later. Too thick? <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span> ice water at a time. Keep it cold.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Make the batter",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Sift the cake flour and starch.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/5-how1.webp?v=fae45742fb"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Add ice water, vinegar and sake; mix only briefly — lumps are fine.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/5-how2.webp?v=17e681c492"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/5.webp?v=5a83474553",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": "Shrimp tempura",
   "part_id": "part-shrimp-tempura",
   "time": "~4 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~4 min</span>",
   "title": "Make the batter",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ cup</span>",
     "name_html": "Cake flour"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Potato starch or cornstarch (batter)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Check the oil: a chopstick dipped in it should get a ring of small bubbles.</li><li>Hold a shrimp by the tail, coat it in batter (the tail stays bare) and lower it in. Fry until golden, <b>about 2 minutes</b>. A few at a time — don’t crowd the pot.</li><li>Drain on a wire rack. Skim the loose crumbs out of the oil between batches before they burn.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
