    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/7.webp?v=da0bc241b9",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": "Shrimp tempura",
   "part_id": "part-shrimp-tempura",
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Dip in mentsuyu",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Mentsuyu (concentrated noodle soup base)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Turn the hot rice into a large bowl to cool a little: <b>warm</b>, cool enough to hold.</li><li>Set out a small bowl of water and a little salt. Wet your hands and rub a pinch of salt over your palms — for flavour, and it helps the rice balls keep.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Warm rice, wet and salted hands",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wet your hands and rub a pinch of salt over your palms.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/8-how1.webp?v=b04afc08cd"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/8.webp?v=6aa1cf4689",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Tenmusu",
   "part_id": "part-tenmusu",
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Warm rice, wet and salted hands",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a small bowl",
     "name_html": "Water (for your hands)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a little",
     "name_html": "Diamond Crystal kosher salt"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Scoop about one rice paddle of rice (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"55\" data-s=\"0\">55 g</span>) into your left palm.</li><li>Press a small well into the middle and lay one tempura in it, <b>tail up</b>, so the tail will stick out of the top.</li><li>Give it one quick, gentle squeeze to bring it together — like making a snowball.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rice, well, shrimp",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "One paddle of rice in your palm, a well in the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/9-how1.webp?v=6e9732690c"
     },
     {
      "caption": "The tempura goes in tail up; one gentle squeeze, like a snowball.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/9-how2.webp?v=a13e58df2f"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/9.webp?v=0ae5d5c2ec",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Tenmusu",
   "part_id": "part-tenmusu",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Rice, well, shrimp",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Bend your right hand into a “roof” over the top and press gently with the fingers and the heel of the hand, turning the ball to make three corners — the tail comes out of the top corner.</li><li>Never squeeze hard: it should hold together, not be packed.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Shape the triangle",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Right hand makes a roof over the top; press gently, turn, three corners.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/10-how1.webp?v=b3cb41826c"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/10.webp?v=3812f4d099",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 10,
   "part": "Tenmusu",
   "part_id": "part-tenmusu",
   "time": null,
   "time_html": null,
   "title": "Shape the triangle",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut each nori sheet into 4 strips (12 strips).</li><li>Lay a strip <b>rough side up</b> (the shiny side ends up outside) and set a tenmusu on its middle.</li><li>Fold both ends up and in toward the centre of the front so they cross like a kimono collar — a V-neck under the tail.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-11",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap in a nori kimono",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cut each nori sheet into 4 strips.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/11-how1.webp?v=a6b6a7be57"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Rough side up, tenmusu in the middle; fold both ends up across the front like a kimono collar.",
      "src": "illustrations/tenmusu/11-how2.webp?v=a9ec049bfb"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tenmusu/11.webp?v=7a43ef88a9",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 11,
   "part": "Tenmusu",
   "part_id": "part-tenmusu",
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap in a nori kimono",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"3\" data-f=\"sheet|sheets\" data-n=\"1\">3 sheets</span>",
     "name_html": "Nori"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Eat right away, or within a few hours — wrapped in plastic and then a thick kitchen towel.</li><li>Don’t refrigerate: the rice turns hard.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
